{"reference":"Psalms 44","book":"Psalms","chapter":44,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Lament and Faithful Speech","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Psalm 44 remembers God’s past help and trustworthiness, yet openly protests present suffering and asks God to act. It shows that within the Psalms, lament, petition, trust, thanksgiving, and praise can stand together; praise is not the only faithful way to address God.","verse_refs":["Psalms 44:1-26"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_044_2fe61f4b512166e32061dd72"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}